== Firmware updates ==

Lamps update themselves from GitHub releases. A lamp checks 15 seconds after
joining WiFi, once a day at 15:00 local, and whenever asked.

<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
./scripts/find_devices.sh --update                     # every lamp with an update
curl -X POST http://castor-lamp.local/api/ota/update   # one lamp: check, install if newer
</syntaxhighlight>

<code>/api/ota/update</code> is the scheduler's endpoint: it does nothing at all on a
lamp that is current, so it is safe to fire at every lamp nightly.

A lamp stops answering for 10&ndash;30 seconds while it downloads, then reboots.

=== Cutting a release ===

<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
# bump FIRMWARE_VERSION in src/version.h first, and commit
./scripts/release.sh 0.0.6
./scripts/find_devices.sh --update
</syntaxhighlight>

The script refuses to tag if the version does not match <code>src/version.h</code>, if the
working tree is dirty, or if the binary would overflow the 1,966,080-byte OTA
slot &mdash; a build that overflows uploads fine over USB and then fails silently
over the air.

'''Cut the release before flashing a new version by hand.''' Versions are compared by
tag equality, not ordering, so a lamp running firmware newer than the latest
release will quietly install the older one. That also makes re-tagging an older
release a supported way to roll back.

== Building ==

<syntaxhighlight lang="bash">
pio run                      # release, the build that ships
pio run -e esp32c3-debug     # verbose logging, USB only
pio run -t upload            # flash over USB
pio device monitor           # 115200
</syntaxhighlight>

Copy <code>lib/Config/Config.h.sample</code> to <code>lib/Config/Config.h</code> before the first
build. It is gitignored and holds the device name and the OTA repo; there are no
secrets in it.

== Troubleshooting ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Symptom !! Cause
|-
| Lamp not found by a scan || mDNS does not cross VLANs. An unprovisioned lamp is not on the network at all &mdash; look for its setup AP.
|-
| A scan lists lamps that do not exist || Stale mDNS records from a rename, cached by the browsing machine. They expire on their own.
|-
| <code>.local</code> name does not resolve || A cold mDNS cache can take longer to answer than a short HTTP timeout. The scripts resolve to an address first for this reason.
|-
| Entity never appears in Home Assistant || The lamp is not connected to the broker &mdash; check the MQTT line on its settings page.
|-
| Entity stuck "unavailable" || The lamp is down, or pointed at a different broker.
|-
| MQTT commands do nothing || <code>state</code> must be <code>"ON"</code>, not <code>true</code>.
|-
| Lamp reverts after every reconnect || A retained message on the command topic. Clear it with <code>mosquitto_pub -r -n -t glowlamp/<host>/set</code>.
|-
| Ring looks washed out or white || Colors too far apart on the wheel in ''flicker'', which mixes by design. Use colors that are close together.
|}

